#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:686
msgid ":pep:`784`."
msgstr ":pep:`784`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:692
msgid "Asyncio introspection capabilities"
msgstr "Möglichkeiten zur Introspektion in asyncio"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:694
msgid ""
"Added a new command-line interface to inspect running Python processes using "
"asynchronous tasks, available via ``python -m asyncio ps PID`` or ``python "
"-m asyncio pstree PID``."
msgstr ""
"Eine neue Befehlszeilenschnittstelle ist hinzugekommen, mit der sich "
"laufende Python-Prozesse untersuchen lassen, die asynchrone Aufträge "
"verwenden. Verfügbar über ``python -m asyncio ps PID`` oder ``python -m "
"asyncio pstree PID``."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:698
msgid ""
"The ``ps`` subcommand inspects the given process ID (PID) and displays "
"information about currently running asyncio tasks. It outputs a task table: "
"a flat listing of all tasks, their names, their coroutine stacks, and which "
"tasks are awaiting them."
msgstr ""
"Der Unterbefehl ``ps`` untersucht die angegebene Prozesskennung (PID) und "
"zeigt Informationen über die derzeit laufenden asyncio-Aufträge an. Er gibt "
"eine Auftragstabelle aus: eine flache Auflistung aller Aufträge, ihrer "
"Namen, ihrer Coroutine-Stapel und derjenigen Aufträge, die auf sie warten."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:704
msgid ""
"The ``pstree`` subcommand fetches the same information, but instead renders "
"a visual async call tree, showing coroutine relationships in a hierarchical "
"format. This command is particularly useful for debugging long-running or "
"stuck asynchronous programs. It can help developers quickly identify where a "
"program is blocked, what tasks are pending, and how coroutines are chained "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Der Unterbefehl ``pstree`` holt dieselben Informationen, stellt aber "
"stattdessen einen anschaulichen asynchronen Aufrufbaum dar, der die "
"Beziehungen der Coroutinen hierarchisch zeigt. Dieser Befehl ist besonders "
"nützlich, um lange laufende oder hängende asynchrone Programme zu "
"untersuchen. Er hilft Entwicklern, schnell zu erkennen, wo ein Programm "
"blockiert, welche Aufträge noch ausstehen und wie die Coroutinen "
"aneinandergekettet sind."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:711
msgid "For example given this code:"
msgstr "Zum Beispiel bei diesem Code:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.14.rst:713
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"async def play_track(track):\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(f'🎵 Finished: {track}')\n"
"\n"
"async def play_album(name, tracks):\n"
"    async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\n"
"        for track in tracks:\n"
"            tg.create_task(play_track(track), name=track)\n"
"\n"
"async def main():\n"
"    async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\n"
"        tg.create_task(\n"
"          play_album('Sundowning', ['TNDNBTG', 'Levitate']),\n"
"          name='Sundowning')\n"
"        tg.create_task(\n"
"          play_album('TMBTE', ['DYWTYLM', 'Aqua Regia']),\n"
"          name='TMBTE')\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    asyncio.run(main())"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"async def play_track(track):\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(5)\n"
"    print(f'🎵 Finished: {track}')\n"
"\n"
"async def play_album(name, tracks):\n"
"    async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\n"
"        for track in tracks:\n"
"            tg.create_task(play_track(track), name=track)\n"
"\n"
"async def main():\n"
"    async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\n"
"        tg.create_task(\n"
"          play_album('Sundowning', ['TNDNBTG', 'Levitate']),\n"
"          name='Sundowning')\n"
"        tg.create_task(\n"
"          play_album('TMBTE', ['DYWTYLM', 'Aqua Regia']),\n"
"          name='TMBTE')\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    asyncio.run(main())"

